  "worked_solution": "If $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical coordinates of a point and $(x,y,z)$ are the corresponding Cartesian coordinates of that point, then we have\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nNow, a point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nf=\u27e8x,\\,y,\\,z\u27e9=\u27e8r\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ,\\,r\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ,\\,z\u27e9.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $z=5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ,$ we obtain the parametrization \n\n$$\nf(r,\\theta )=\u27e8r\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ,\\,r\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ,\\,5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \u27e9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is  $r\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta .$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
